  "scope": "Exact43 new ticket17 raw-retention frontdoor files only; source2306/docs295 unchanged; B not read.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "T17-RETENTION-STANDARDS-01",
      "priority": "P2",
      "classification": "documented-standard breach",
      "file": ".scratch/barness-ai-minimax/evidence/ticket-17/freeze.py",
      "line": 27,
      "additionalLines": [
        68,
        69
      ],
      "rule": "AGENTS.md4 treats every external input as untrusted and requires safe default boundaries;5 requires bounded failure/resource behavior;9 requires safe verifiable changes. The local failure inventory promises regular/no-follow/finite snapshot reads.",
      "quote": "v=json.loads((RAW/label/'command.json').read_bytes())",
      "finding": "The earlier scandir lstat/size observation does not protect a subsequent pathname open/read. These direct reads bypass read(path), which uses the existing component-wise no-follow/nonblocking regular-FD reader and a size/cumulative read cap. The raw command file can be replaced or grow between scan and read, causing link traversal, FIFO blocking or unbounded allocation. The final Path.read_bytes() source-proof reread and file_digest archive reread have the same bypass.",
      "requestedChange": "Move/reuse the existing finite same-FD metadata reader before command validation and use it for every source-proof reread. Hash the archive through component-wise no-follow regular FD, fstat expected/cap guard and cumulative byte count; preserve historical raw/archive/inventory/native pins and all fixed reader limits. Add failure-first public creator guard receipts on private copies without executing captured code.",
      "notClaimed": "No defect found in unchanged pinned full reader, actual original capsule custody, typed numeric command checks or source/doc qualification; no current raw corruption or new native certification is inferred."
    }
  ],
  "smells": [],
  "standards": [
    "AGENTS.md principles1-10 and failure-first public E2E requirements.",
    "Twelve supplied smell heuristics assessed as judgments; documented repo rules override; no tooling-enforced issue reported.",
    "Existing full retention protocol is reused without widened bounds; source/history/current-certification separation applies."
  ],
  "report": "CHANGES_REQUESTED: one documented boundary breach remains in the new retention creator; no baseline smell is reported. T17-RETENTION-STANDARDS-01: freeze.py reads raw command metadata with Path.read_bytes() after its directory scan, then repeats unbounded pathname reads for source-proof and archive hashing. A replacement FIFO/link or growing regular input can bypass the existing no-follow/nonblocking/regular-file and finite-read guards. Reuse the existing same-FD bounded reader for metadata and bound compressed archive hashing on the opened regular FD. This concerns creator safety; the public verification reader remains bounded.\n\nIndependent stdlib streaming checked all62996 regular members,106602 physical headers,594764048 payload bytes and all39321 artifact references. All1642 fixture inputs were checked, including141 exact same-stage anthropic/failures.json input-to-saved-artifact relationships; none was ignored or accepted by arbitrary hash similarity. All88 selected resource records are zero.\n\nTwenty-four numeric command stages preserve genuine42 malformed sends at1Provider/1Attempt, then42 local0/0 rejections plus2 business-wire positives. Ordinary/race remain1663 PASS+8 NOT_RUN each; separate exact8 opt-ins each PASS. Six measured ca67+WIP snapshots match1027 Git2306 compiler/JSON/modsum files, without claiming a postcommit1056 operational freeze. Compile, fixture, dependency, initial reader/authoring failures and the non-authoritative2548-byte archive remain distinct. Original source/docs/applicability review bytes are preserved. Recorded public verification0 and11 private-copy refusals were read, not rerun. No credential/network/project execution or repository/raw write occurred; no current formal eligibility or paid authority is granted.",
